    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "description": "For cedar's failed GitHub V2 setup, trigger-worker appears to use an obsolete setup path (/webhook_endpoints) instead of the supported V2 trigger-instance upsert path, so the observed failure is best explained as an internal migrated-path/configuration problem rather than GitHub credentials or a broad provider outage.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_fc893edaf1b0",
          "ev_3ef242d960a6",
          "ev_585556a216e4",
          "ev_229014d4d4bb",
          "ev_abce4cfbe569"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [],
        "confidence": "high",
        "assumptions": [
          "The production log field attempted_setup_path reflects the path actually selected by the GitHub V2 setup flow.",
          "The controlled sandbox comparison verifies path/configuration sensitivity but does not prove every production condition.",
          "The exact source of the 404 is not directly observed in canonical egress telemetry."
        ]
      },
      {
        "description": "A provider-surface failure remains possible because the observed setup attempt returned 404 before trigger creation, but current evidence supports this less strongly than an internal obsolete-path problem.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_fc893edaf1b0"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [
          "ev_3ef242d960a6",
          "ev_35d387f6c8dc",
          "ev_585556a216e4",
          "ev_abce4cfbe569"
        ],
        "confidence": "low",
        "assumptions": [
          "The 404 could have originated from a GitHub-facing intermediary rather than purely internal validation.",
          "Missing canonical egress traces mean provider contact cannot be fully confirmed or excluded."
        ]
      },
      {
        "description": "A GitHub organization approval or permission issue is theoretically possible for a connected account, but the supplied evidence does not specifically support org approval, scope, or resource authorization as the leading explanation for the observed cedar failure.",
        "supporting_evidence": [],
        "contradicting_evidence": [
          "ev_fc893edaf1b0",
          "ev_3ef242d960a6",
          "ev_35d387f6c8dc"
        ],
        "confidence": "low",
        "assumptions": [
          "auth_valid=true shows valid authentication but not complete authorization for every org or repo.",
          "No canonical provider error body or resource-authorization record is present to verify an approval problem."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "recommended_actions": [
      "Use canonical request/response telemetry to verify whether cedar's GitHub V2 setup path selection should have been /trigger_instances/{slug}/upsert rather than /webhook_endpoints; recommended actions have not been executed.",
      "Collect missing synthetic telemetry for req-37: upstream 404 body, any egress attempt, and the exact internal branch/configuration that selected the setup path.",
      "Use the supplied controlled reproduction as a regression check for migrated GitHub V2 setup path selection.",
      "Monitor for any concurrent GitHub-facing 404s on the same setup surface before broadening this incident to provider instability.",
      "If the path-selection explanation is disproved, then inspect canonical authorization telemetry for the exact GitHub org/repo to test for organization approval or resource-access blocking."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Synthetic telemetry is incomplete: there is no canonical provider-egress trace, upstream error body, or explicit production record naming the migration branch used by req-37.",
      "Tenant metrics show cedar severity and backlog but are service/tenant level, not proof that all cedar failures in the window shared this exact mechanism.",
      "The sandbox controlled comparison is strong discriminating evidence for path/configuration, but it is not direct proof of all production-side conditions.",
      "The empty github-filtered dependency query cannot prove absence of a dependency-specific condition."
    ]
  },
